WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.600
Nice.

3
00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:21.229
Argh.

4
00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.197
Nice.

5
00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:33.824
Oh...

6
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.368
Somebody's ready for action.

7
00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.997
It smells delicious in here.
Did you cut yourself?

8
00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:41.833
Just testing it. It works.

9
00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.626
You brought Mr. Ball Legs home?

10
00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:47.213
Yeah. I thought maybe a change
of scenery would cheer him up.

11
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.090
Maybe he would enjoy Bangkok.

12
00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:51.384
Is that Ramona's ball creature?

13
00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:52.509
Cool.

14
00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:59.059
It's like when we go to the zoo
and none of the animals give a fuck.

15
00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:03.313
So I ran into Lisa...
and she had some big news.

16
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.690
About a certain girl...

17
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:07.192
and a certain boy.

18
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.734
Dating.

19
00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.821
One of them's named Abby.

20
00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:15.784
You're no fun.

21
00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.994
Are you dating Eric?

22
00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.580
That is so cute.

23
00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.248
Oh. God! We're not dating.

24
00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:24.209
Whatever you kids call it today.

25
00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:25.710
"Smashing."

26
00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:28.004
Mom! Never be in public.

27
00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.341
It was a stupid misunderstanding.
I can't believe Lisa's telling people.

28
00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.759
So. you're not dating?

29
00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.844
Or... "hooking"?

30
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:36.971
Oh. my God! Goodbye!

31
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.267
I don't care if it's not true.
We are not letting this go.

32
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:44.479
Ready to go deal with your friend

33
00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:46.898
- who left a knife in our door?
- Yes.

34
00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:48.566
Let me just grab his address.

35
00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.695
And Ron's not my friend. We just...

36
00:01:53.404 --> 00:01:56.908
shared a room in a mental hospital.
where I told him my deepest secrets

37
00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:58.993
and comforted him when he cried.

38
00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:01.496
Oh. shit. We're friends.

39
00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.131
I hope we don't have to kill Ron.
He seems sweet.

40
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:14.551
People can be sweet and dangerous.
Example. us. Also. koala bears.

41
00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:15.844
Ding dong!

42
00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:20.515
Outside? You say "ding dong" outside?

43
00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.061
We heard you guys are starting
your own realty company. Big yay.

44
00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.981
And we wanted to mark the occasion
with a dolce de leche cake.

45
00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:30.150
But they didn't have one.
so we got you monkey bread.

46
00:02:31.609 --> 00:02:33.570
- That is so nice.
- So nice.

47
00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.947
We know how hard it can be to strike out
on your own.

48
00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:38.616
Yeah. we've been there.
and we were young when we did it.

49
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.410
We're still young.

50
00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.661
Yes. you are.

51
00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.164
- No. we are
- Yes. you are.

52
00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:47.167
Say. while we're here...
we heard from Judy Humbolt

53
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.878
and she said you wanted to list
you six-bedroom Mediterranean?

54
00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:51.754
Very high-end. Good for you.

55
00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:54.507
It's like a couple of ants
trying to lift a cornflake.

56
00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:56.399
We just don't want you
to waste your time

57
00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:59.053
because high-end neighborhoods
are kind of our thing.

58
00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.807
Why are you smiling. pretty lady?

59
00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:04.809
'Cause I just realized
why you came over here

60
00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:06.811
and it's flattering.
You're threatened by us.

61
00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:07.937
Oh. yes.

62
00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:11.316
Your monkey bread smells of fear.

63
00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.902
We just didn't want to get crushed by us.

64
00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:17.280
Maybe you should be selling the type
of home you're more familiar with.

65
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.115
Like your cute little starter here.

66
00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.743
We're not gonna get crushed.
We're gonna drag that cornflake

67
00:03:21.826 --> 00:03:24.370
back to the colony.
stage it with all-white furniture

68
00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.706
and sell it for 10% above asking.

69
00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.459
Yeah. We are gonna get that listing.

70
00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:31.502
Judy Humbolt and I go way back.

71
00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.463
Once at summer camp. she got homesick

72
00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.924
so I stayed up all night
braiding her hair.

73
00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:37.007
Aw...

74
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.929
I finger-banged her into her first orgasm
at her brother's Bar Mitzvah party.

75
00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.681
L'chaim. bitches.

76
00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:44.848
Hey. guys!

77
00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:48.228
I'm not liking the body language
over here. Everything alright?

78
00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:50.772
- It's fine. We were ju...
- Not talking to you. sir.

79
00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:51.940
This is ridiculous.

80
00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.610
Ma'am. why don't you take a seat
on the pavement for me?

81
00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:56.735
Are you serious?

82
00:03:57.445 --> 00:03:58.445
Ma'am?

83
00:04:05.203 --> 00:04:06.037
Sheila?

84
00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.206
Our friends from Principal Residential

85
00:04:08.289 --> 00:04:11.793
thought they could come here and tell us
where we can and cannot sell homes.

86
00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:13.086
Well. that doesn't seem right.

87
00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:14.420
This is Officer Garcia.

88
00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:17.090
She's our sheriff friend. She has a gun.

89
00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:20.176
I'm an enormous man.
I'm not afraid of her.

90
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.137
Cool. Why don't I turn off my body cam?
We'll see where this goes.

91
00:04:23.221 --> 00:04:24.221
Stop.

92
00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:26.933
You will not fight. That is a $1.500 suit.

93
00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:29.519
Yeah. You're lucky I'm not wearing
an outfit

94
00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.854
like Joel you buy at a grocery store.

95
00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:34.482
Look who's afraid to punch a cop.

96
00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:35.565
We're leaving.

97
00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.902
And we're taking back our monkey bread.

98
00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.540
Thank you. Anne.

99
00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.292
I serve Him by serving you.

100
00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:54.752
The shield of righteousness never falters.

101
00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.088
Alrighty.

102
00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:04.470
Okay. I know things aren't perfect
with Anne. but you have to admit...

103
00:05:04.554 --> 00:05:05.638
that was pretty cool.

104
00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:07.932
That was... kinda cool.

105
00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:11.436
Christa was so cocky and then she was.
like. "Whaa?"

106
00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:12.645
And Chris was all...

107
00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:15.690
Maybe we should bring Anne to see Ron.

108
00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:17.942
and if he's a problem.
she could back his ass down.

109
00:05:18.109 --> 00:05:20.445
I don't think that's a good idea.
She's kind of wild card.

110
00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.030
She took our Nazi yesterday.

111
00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:24.490
Yeah. Well. it was her first day
on the job.

112
00:05:24.615 --> 00:05:26.367
But. that was terrible.

113
00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:30.121
Can you believe that douchebag

114
00:05:30.204 --> 00:05:32.040
spends $1.500 on a suit?

115
00:05:34.876 --> 00:05:37.045
You want to have a $1.500 suit. don't you?

116
00:05:37.128 --> 00:05:38.128
I would wear one.

117
00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.592
We have a problem.

118
00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.739
Remember when Sven and I went
to the fracking site on our date?

119
00:05:46.095 --> 00:05:47.513
Oh. my God. You're pregnant.

120
00:05:48.264 --> 00:05:49.640
Yes. and it's triplets.

121
00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:51.726
I'm naming them Hey. Idiot
and Pay Attention.

122
00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.644
- Okay.
- Nothing happened with Sven.

123
00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.105
But those pictures we took
so I could scout the site?

124
00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:57.899
He just posted them on Instagram.

125
00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:01.569
"Wow. can't believe
I was at the fracking site

126
00:06:01.652 --> 00:06:04.072
with Abby Hammond
days before the terrorist attack."

127
00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:05.531
Hashtag brush with death.

128
00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:08.451
Hashtag makes you think.
hashtag these colors don't run.

129
00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:11.579
This is bad. This puts me
at the crime scene

130
00:06:11.662 --> 00:06:14.165
- taking photos like I'm casing it.
- Which you were.

131
00:06:14.248 --> 00:06:16.834
It would be great if the FBI
didn't know that.

132
00:06:17.335 --> 00:06:18.895
We have to get Sven to take these down.

133
00:06:19.003 --> 00:06:21.923
Definitely. Oh. also.
we should get rid of my backpack.

134
00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:24.092
We had the C4 in it
so there's probably residue.

135
00:06:24.175 --> 00:06:27.762
I'll do that. You deal with Sven.
He and I didn't end on the best terms.

136
00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:30.556
Sure. Want me to rough him up
or just talk to him?

137
00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.970
Keep in mind I'm only capable
of one of those things.

138
00:06:33.017 --> 00:06:34.017
You'll do great.

139
00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.188
Hey. speaking of our web of deception...

140
00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:40.691
Your mom told my parents
that we're in a relationship.

141
00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:41.818
What did Joel think?

142
00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:44.695
Yeah. my point is. can you please ask
her not to tell anyone else?

143
00:06:44.987 --> 00:06:46.781
It's just... I'd like
to keep this contained.

144
00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.825
Sure. I'll tell her.

145
00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:50.827
Does it make you uncomfortable?

146
00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.079
It's not you. It's just...

147
00:06:53.162 --> 00:06:55.832
I have so many lies on my plate.
I really can't handle another one.

148
00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.208
Totally get it. No worries.

149
00:06:57.291 --> 00:06:59.211
No one but our parents
will think we're together.

150
00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.754
- Thank you.
- Except my mom already told my grandma.

151
00:07:02.338 --> 00:07:03.923
She wants to give you her ring.

152
00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:12.640
Do you really think Ron could be
a Knight of Serbia?

153
00:07:12.807 --> 00:07:14.142
Or maybe he just thinks he is.

154
00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:16.227
Either way. we should be prepared.

155
00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:18.145
Argh.

156
00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:19.688
Fuck this thing.

157
00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:22.066
I told you I'd knit you a cover.

158
00:07:24.652 --> 00:07:26.154
Joel? Oh!

159
00:07:28.406 --> 00:07:29.949
I was so worried about you.

160
00:07:30.032 --> 00:07:31.367
I was a little worried too. Ron.

161
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.287
- Hi. Sheila.
- Hi. Ron.

162
00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.165
Come in. It's so good to see you guys.

163
00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:42.170
So... What brings you here?

164
00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:43.546
Hm...

165
00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.423
The knife you stuck in our door

166
00:07:45.506 --> 00:07:47.884
with the note that said.
"Beware. the knights are coming."

167
00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:49.407
I didn't stick a knife in your door.

168
00:07:49.594 --> 00:07:51.387
It had your fingerprints on it.

169
00:07:52.388 --> 00:07:55.475
Okay. I did stick a knife in your door.
I wanted to warn you

170
00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:58.394
your lives were in danger
but I didn't want you to know it was me

171
00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.897
because I'm the one who put your lives
in danger.

172
00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.273
Does anyone want tea?

173
00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.525
No tea. What did you do. Ron?

174
00:08:04.609 --> 00:08:07.653
Okay. I met this guy Paul
through a paranormal subreddit

175
00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:10.615
and I told him... What's in the satchel?

176
00:08:11.407 --> 00:08:13.951
Don't worry about that. You told him...

177
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.160
Right.

178
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.372
Sorry. Now all I can think about
is the satchel.

179
00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.625
Ron! We need you to focus here.

180
00:08:20.791 --> 00:08:21.791
You got it.

181
00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:23.628
- Ron!
- I'm with you!

182
00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:26.506
Here... Look.

183
00:08:27.298 --> 00:08:30.301
It's just a hammer knife...
in case we have to kill you.

184
00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.387
Thank you. That was going
to drive me crazy.

185
00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.473
Please. sit.

186
00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.770
So... This guy Paul.

187
00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:44.232
Yeah. He has this weird spider-like thing
tattooed on his arm.

188
00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.357
Mr. Ball Legs.

189
00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:46.484
What's that?

190
00:08:46.651 --> 00:08:48.194
Doesn't matter. Go on.

191
00:08:48.277 --> 00:08:49.277
Okay.

192
00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:53.407
I can't.

193
00:08:53.491 --> 00:08:56.702
Fine. When you become undead.
you throw up a pod...

194
00:08:56.911 --> 00:08:59.580
and it eventually turns
into an eight-legged creature.

195
00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:01.040
That's Mr. Ball Legs.

196
00:09:01.123 --> 00:09:03.167
Thank you. Sheila. See?

197
00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.670
Is it so hard to include me?

198
00:09:05.753 --> 00:09:09.131
So this Paul... Did he say
he was a Knight of Serbia?

199
00:09:10.007 --> 00:09:10.883
Yes.

200
00:09:10.967 --> 00:09:12.176
Holy shit. they're here.

201
00:09:12.301 --> 00:09:15.721
They started hunting the undead
500 years ago. and now they're here.

202
00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:17.598
Do you know how many there are?

203
00:09:17.682 --> 00:09:19.141
Doesn't seem like a lot.

204
00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.425
I think there's just one
for each region of the country.

205
00:09:21.477 --> 00:09:25.565
Paul has California. Arizona
and the Vegas Strip.

206
00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:28.025
Obviously. the Knights are not immune
to gerrymandering.

207
00:09:28.317 --> 00:09:31.571
So... what is it like being undead?

208
00:09:32.113 --> 00:09:34.198
Forget that. What did you tell Paul
about us?

209
00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:39.996
Well. your whole life changes.

210
00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:42.623
It's like that moment in <i>The Wizard of Oz</i>

211
00:09:42.707 --> 00:09:47.420
when the whole world goes
from black and white to... color.

212
00:09:47.712 --> 00:09:48.713
Wow.

213
00:09:49.505 --> 00:09:51.424
That sounds wonderful.

214
00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.218
Yeah. my life has been pretty gray
since my wife died.

215
00:09:54.343 --> 00:09:55.511
We did everything together.

216
00:09:56.971 --> 00:09:58.139
Oh. Ron. I'm so sorry.

217
00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:00.599
That's okay.

218
00:10:01.684 --> 00:10:04.770
So. what is your favorite part
about being immortal?

219
00:10:04.854 --> 00:10:06.814
Are you looking forward
to living on Mars one day?

220
00:10:07.189 --> 00:10:08.649
Wait. Immortal?

221
00:10:09.191 --> 00:10:10.901
Yeah... You're undead.

222
00:10:10.985 --> 00:10:13.029
So unless someone puts a spike
through your head.

223
00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:14.989
you're going to live forever.

224
00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.160
I haven't thought of that.

225
00:10:19.744 --> 00:10:20.828
Neither did I.

226
00:10:21.495 --> 00:10:22.747
That's pretty intense.

227
00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:24.582
You guys. focus!

228
00:10:24.665 --> 00:10:26.208
Paul is trying to kill you!

229
00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:27.960
Right. What did you tell him
about us?

230
00:10:28.085 --> 00:10:31.005
All I said was I know an undead woman...

231
00:10:31.213 --> 00:10:32.590
But nothing about us specifically.

232
00:10:32.715 --> 00:10:34.800
...who's one half of a realtor couple...

233
00:10:34.884 --> 00:10:37.261
- But not where we live.
- ...in Santa Clarita.

234
00:10:39.889 --> 00:10:42.183
So. we go to Paul's. see what he knows.

235
00:10:42.266 --> 00:10:44.786
Right. And then we figure out a way
to throw him off his tracks.

236
00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.090
You know. so he doesn't kill me.

237
00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:47.563
How do we get him to talk to us?

238
00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:50.775
You could pretend to be
a Knight of Serbia...

239
00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.568
visiting from another region.

240
00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:53.652
I could be a Knight.

241
00:10:53.778 --> 00:10:56.238
I did so more tricky legs than anyone
at the Renaissance Fair.

242
00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:57.322
You did.

243
00:10:58.407 --> 00:11:01.118
So... I'm going to live forever.

244
00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:02.870
That's some shit. right?

245
00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.664
Yeah... Hard to imagine.

246
00:11:05.373 --> 00:11:07.750
Although. if Paul recognizes us
from the clam farm...

247
00:11:07.958 --> 00:11:08.959
we could both die today.

248
00:11:09.043 --> 00:11:10.795
I could meet my great-grandchildren

249
00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:12.755
and their great-grandchildren.

250
00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.507
That's so many greats.

251
00:11:14.715 --> 00:11:16.175
What would they even call me?

252
00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.053
- Honey... we have bigger...
- How about Bop bop?

253
00:11:19.595 --> 00:11:21.430
Well. you just add a bop
to every generation.

254
00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:22.848
Of course. pretty soon

255
00:11:22.932 --> 00:11:26.644
I would be Bop bop bop bop bop bop bop
bop bop bop bop bop.

256
00:11:27.103 --> 00:11:28.938
I don't even know how to think about that.

257
00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:30.606
You're talking centuries from now.

258
00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.484
Even if we do survive today.
with all the shit coming at us...

259
00:11:33.567 --> 00:11:35.778
I don't know how we're gonna get
through the year.

260
00:11:35.861 --> 00:11:36.862
Whoa.

261
00:11:38.989 --> 00:11:41.450
Well. let's just focus on today. then.

262
00:11:42.451 --> 00:11:44.704
How are we going to get Paul to believe
you're a Knight?

263
00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:46.539
Still have those fancy colored pens
at home?

264
00:11:46.622 --> 00:11:49.041
Of course. They're at Bop bop's
arts and crafts store.

265
00:11:58.175 --> 00:11:59.927
You're throwing away your backpack?

266
00:12:01.887 --> 00:12:04.014
Yes... as people do.

267
00:12:04.557 --> 00:12:07.226
It looks pretty new.
Why are you getting rid of it?

268
00:12:08.018 --> 00:12:09.770
It was asking too many questions.

269
00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:11.271
I know you.

270
00:12:11.605 --> 00:12:13.941
You were in Environmental Club
for. like. five minutes.

271
00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.318
You're Winter. right?

272
00:12:16.527 --> 00:12:18.154
I saw you at the fundraiser.

273
00:12:18.362 --> 00:12:20.906
You made the lemon squares
that were so good...

274
00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.825
Amanda threw her batch down the stairs.

275
00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.703
Yeah. people think just 'cause I have
a shitty attitude. I can't bake.

276
00:12:25.828 --> 00:12:27.288
People can be more than one thing.

277
00:12:27.371 --> 00:12:29.373
Abraham Lincoln invented the pancake.

278
00:12:31.834 --> 00:12:34.670
If you don't want anyone to find that.
you should cut it up or burn it.

279
00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.470
My dude.

280
00:12:43.679 --> 00:12:46.098
Saw your Instagram
about the fracking site.

281
00:12:46.307 --> 00:12:47.308
Thanks. man.

282
00:12:47.808 --> 00:12:48.808
I'm okay.

283
00:12:49.018 --> 00:12:51.020
Oh. good. We've all been so worried.

284
00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:53.230
But. hey. listen. Those pictures
put you at the site

285
00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:55.417
right before it exploded.
It might look incriminating.

286
00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:56.841
You should probably take them down.

287
00:12:57.276 --> 00:12:58.276
I didn't do anything.

288
00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:00.070
- Might seem like you did.
- But I didn't.

289
00:13:00.988 --> 00:13:02.573
- Might seem...
- But I didn't.

290
00:13:02.656 --> 00:13:03.491
Mm-hmm...

291
00:13:03.574 --> 00:13:06.494
We were just there because Abby
wanted to take pictures.

292
00:13:08.329 --> 00:13:10.456
Wait. Is she the one you're worried about?

293
00:13:10.831 --> 00:13:11.831
Abby? No...

294
00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:13.674
Do you not want people knowing
Abby was there?

295
00:13:13.709 --> 00:13:15.294
Me? No. What? No.

296
00:13:15.503 --> 00:13:17.046
She was acting weird.

297
00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:19.131
At one point. she asked me to move over

298
00:13:19.215 --> 00:13:21.383
like she wanted better pictures
of the site.

299
00:13:21.592 --> 00:13:22.927
Why would she do that unless...

300
00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:24.261
Abby and I are dating. okay?

301
00:13:24.345 --> 00:13:26.430
And seeing photos of you two together
tears me apart

302
00:13:26.597 --> 00:13:28.015
so I need you to take them down.

303
00:13:28.098 --> 00:13:29.183
I'm jealous. Sven.

304
00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:31.727
I hate that I'm like that.
but there it is.

305
00:13:32.019 --> 00:13:33.521
I'm a jealous motherfucker.

306
00:13:34.897 --> 00:13:35.897
Okay.

307
00:13:36.273 --> 00:13:37.733
- I get that.
- Wait!

308
00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:39.527
You're dating Abby Hammond?

309
00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:42.321
Shit... Yeah.

310
00:13:44.156 --> 00:13:45.533
I mean. shit yeah!

311
00:13:55.334 --> 00:13:57.479
We know that Paul is looking
for a realtor couple so...

312
00:13:57.503 --> 00:13:59.213
- I got it.
- And if he recognizes us

313
00:13:59.296 --> 00:14:00.798
- from the clam farm?
- I got it.

314
00:14:02.383 --> 00:14:04.218
Did you really mean what you said before?

315
00:14:04.301 --> 00:14:06.461
That you thought we might not
make it through the year?

316
00:14:06.512 --> 00:14:07.763
Our life is precarious.

317
00:14:08.013 --> 00:14:10.850
Every day. we're one mistake away
from losing everything.

318
00:14:11.308 --> 00:14:13.435
But every day we're still here.
and I think

319
00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:15.229
we're getting better and better at this.

320
00:14:15.521 --> 00:14:16.897
Maybe you're just a pessimist.

321
00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:18.065
Or maybe I'm a realist.

322
00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.460
I did tell you in college
that your Beanie Baby collection

323
00:14:20.484 --> 00:14:23.988
would have no value. so you should just
take the tags off and have fun.

324
00:14:26.657 --> 00:14:27.908
- Hi!
- Hi!

325
00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.450
Are you Paul?

326
00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:32.621
Paul! There's people here to see you!

327
00:14:32.746 --> 00:14:34.290
- Who are they?
- I don't know!

328
00:14:34.498 --> 00:14:36.500
I'm not your fucking butler!

329
00:14:36.917 --> 00:14:38.168
Come in or whatever.

330
00:14:41.463 --> 00:14:44.800
They're loose in the house now.
if you want to come deal with it!

331
00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.178
- Hey.
- Hi.

332
00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.847
We're Belle and Sebastian.

333
00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:51.891
A brother-sister. doctor-nurse team.

334
00:14:52.433 --> 00:14:53.633
What can I do for you. Doctor?

335
00:14:53.767 --> 00:14:55.519
Why do you assume she's the doctor?

336
00:14:55.853 --> 00:14:57.396
- Why wouldn't he?
- It's just...

337
00:14:57.813 --> 00:15:00.024
I'm curious what about me
says nurse to you.

338
00:15:00.107 --> 00:15:02.902
I don't know. Kind eyes.
upper body strength.

339
00:15:03.652 --> 00:15:05.779
Oh. well then. Thank you.

340
00:15:07.364 --> 00:15:08.616
Did you two want something?

341
00:15:08.699 --> 00:15:10.826
We're in town visiting from the Midwest

342
00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:14.496
and we just wanted to stop by
and congratulate the man

343
00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.582
who blew up that clam farm.

344
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.376
How do you know about that?

345
00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.003
Because you and I...

346
00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:22.922
have something in common.

347
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:28.802
How's it going?

348
00:15:30.971 --> 00:15:31.971
Oh. my God.

349
00:15:32.014 --> 00:15:34.767
I've never met another
Knight of Serbia before.

350
00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.728
I mean. I exchanged pie recipes once
with a Knight in Florida.

351
00:15:37.811 --> 00:15:39.688
but she went paleo and then we lost touch.

352
00:15:41.398 --> 00:15:42.524
Oh. my goodness.

353
00:15:44.109 --> 00:15:45.527
Please. sit. Have a seat.

354
00:15:46.195 --> 00:15:47.279
Sorry about the mess.

355
00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:52.201
I'm meeting my girlfriend Marsha
in Hawaii. We're going to start a family.

356
00:15:53.494 --> 00:15:56.413
Great news! Congratulations!

357
00:15:57.081 --> 00:15:58.082
So that's it. then?

358
00:15:58.165 --> 00:16:00.376
You won't be hunting the undead anymore?

359
00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:03.170
No. I'm hanging up my rocket launcher.
which is a good thing

360
00:16:03.253 --> 00:16:05.297
because the rockets are stupid expensive

361
00:16:05.381 --> 00:16:08.425
and you have to buy them from. like...
the worst people.

362
00:16:09.551 --> 00:16:11.637
Paul's leaving town to start a family.

363
00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:12.805
How romantic.

364
00:16:13.806 --> 00:16:15.724
Do you see why I'm an optimist. bro?

365
00:16:18.811 --> 00:16:20.187
Tommy. god dammit!

366
00:16:21.271 --> 00:16:22.356
You had a moth.

367
00:16:23.899 --> 00:16:25.818
You come into my house...

368
00:16:26.151 --> 00:16:28.654
and you try to eat my wounds?

369
00:16:28.946 --> 00:16:30.114
Fuck you!

370
00:16:33.867 --> 00:16:36.120
You've met met my unpleasant brother
Tommy.

371
00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:38.080
He used to be a sniper in the Army.

372
00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:41.500
But now he's going to take over for me
as the new Knight of Serbia.

373
00:16:42.042 --> 00:16:44.628
So the guy who exchanged
pie recipes is out

374
00:16:44.712 --> 00:16:47.506
and the professional sharpshooter is in.

375
00:16:47.756 --> 00:16:48.756
Yay.

376
00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.260
Hey.

377
00:16:52.344 --> 00:16:54.763
So. I cut the backpack into pieces

378
00:16:54.847 --> 00:16:57.725
and put the pieces in separate dumpsters.
Smart. right?

379
00:16:57.891 --> 00:17:00.291
- How'd it go with Sven?
- I got him to take down the photos.

380
00:17:00.352 --> 00:17:01.992
And that's the victory we should focus on

381
00:17:02.062 --> 00:17:04.481
while I tell you this other really funny
thing that happened.

382
00:17:04.773 --> 00:17:05.773
Oh. my God.

383
00:17:05.899 --> 00:17:08.527
I just heard from Emily
that you have a boyfriend...

384
00:17:08.986 --> 00:17:10.696
- and it's this guy.
- Eric.

385
00:17:11.739 --> 00:17:14.116
Oh. my God. He is in love with you.

386
00:17:14.908 --> 00:17:17.202
Yeah. it's all happening so fast.

387
00:17:17.286 --> 00:17:18.495
Which can be explained.

388
00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:21.540
I want what you have.

389
00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.419
- What the hell?
- Sven was getting suspicious.

390
00:17:25.502 --> 00:17:28.505
I had said I was jealous about the
pictures to get him to take them down.

391
00:17:28.589 --> 00:17:30.632
But now the whole school
thinks we're dating.

392
00:17:30.758 --> 00:17:31.758
So?

393
00:17:32.217 --> 00:17:34.344
Is the idea of being with me
that embarrassing to you?

394
00:17:34.428 --> 00:17:35.763
- No!
- Then why are you so upset?

395
00:17:35.888 --> 00:17:38.199
Because it's like all these events
keep pushing us together

396
00:17:38.223 --> 00:17:39.349
and I'm not ready.

397
00:17:42.436 --> 00:17:44.146
If we ever do get together.
I want it to be

398
00:17:44.229 --> 00:17:45.773
because both of us choose it.

399
00:17:47.691 --> 00:17:48.691
I understand.

400
00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.610
I'm sorry.

401
00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.570
Thank you.

402
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:54.782
"Ever do get together"?

403
00:17:54.865 --> 00:17:56.492
- Eric...
- No. sorry. I get it.

404
00:17:58.827 --> 00:18:00.120
And I'm sick of it!

405
00:18:02.956 --> 00:18:05.209
- What?
- We're done.

406
00:18:05.542 --> 00:18:07.294
I'm breaking up with you. Abby.

407
00:18:08.962 --> 00:18:10.339
You're breaking up with me?

408
00:18:10.464 --> 00:18:12.091
I heard they're having problems.

409
00:18:12.174 --> 00:18:13.217
I'm sorry.

410
00:18:13.509 --> 00:18:16.553
I tried to make it work. but I can't be
with just one female.

411
00:18:17.471 --> 00:18:19.681
I'm like a blue tongue skink. in that way.

412
00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.685
God. I'm going to miss your deep.
sexy knowledge of lizards.

413
00:18:24.853 --> 00:18:25.853
Goodbye.

414
00:18:28.857 --> 00:18:30.359
Sorry. y'all had to see that.

415
00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.120
Excuse me. Could you direct me
to Principal Novak's office?

416
00:18:41.787 --> 00:18:42.996
Yeah. just down the hall

417
00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.873
you make a right and then a left...

418
00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:47.543
Whoa. You have a gun.
Are you here to arrest him?

419
00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.921
Is he the guy who robbed a Starbucks
wearing that mascot costume?

420
00:18:51.713 --> 00:18:53.841
I don't know anything about that.
I'm with the FBI.

421
00:18:57.136 --> 00:19:00.180
So... tell us about when you blew up
the clam farm.

422
00:19:00.389 --> 00:19:01.640
What did you see that night?

423
00:19:01.723 --> 00:19:03.225
I'd heard about an undead woman...

424
00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.602
and I think she was there.
running from the explosion.

425
00:19:05.769 --> 00:19:07.146
- No.
- Yeah.

426
00:19:07.271 --> 00:19:10.232
She was a short blonde woman
with a taller man.

427
00:19:10.732 --> 00:19:12.234
It was pretty dark out...

428
00:19:12.609 --> 00:19:14.653
but I'd know them if I saw them again.

429
00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.322
Hey...

430
00:19:20.033 --> 00:19:21.743
I never offered you guys a drink.

431
00:19:22.411 --> 00:19:23.411
Oh!

432
00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:24.872
We're fine. thanks.

433
00:19:24.955 --> 00:19:27.124
So. this undead woman
you're looking for...

434
00:19:27.416 --> 00:19:28.417
What's your plan?

435
00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.500
He doesn't have one.

436
00:19:29.543 --> 00:19:32.713
This is the first undead sighting
in 50 years

437
00:19:32.796 --> 00:19:34.840
and this needle dick's running off
to Hawaii.

438
00:19:34.965 --> 00:19:37.634
Because I'm in love and I get to be happy.

439
00:19:37.718 --> 00:19:40.012
And the plan is
that you are going to apply yourself

440
00:19:40.095 --> 00:19:43.557
for the first time in your life
and track this woman down.

441
00:19:43.891 --> 00:19:47.311
Now. we know that she and her husband
are realtors in Santa Clarita.

442
00:19:47.978 --> 00:19:48.978
Hey.

443
00:19:49.229 --> 00:19:51.231
We're going to be in town
for a little while.

444
00:19:51.356 --> 00:19:53.483
We could help you find
this realtor couple.

445
00:19:53.567 --> 00:19:55.986
Yeah. We could even kill her for you.

446
00:19:56.236 --> 00:19:58.655
Wow. This plan's really coming together.

447
00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.950
No. You can find her. but I want
to shoot the brain out of her skull

448
00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.874
and then I'm gonna find that freaky
little spider thing and I'm gonna...

449
00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.121
keep it as a pet.

450
00:20:07.789 --> 00:20:09.791
It's called a maladragon. dummy.

451
00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:11.335
Which you would know. had you read

452
00:20:11.501 --> 00:20:13.045
any of the sacred texts.

453
00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:14.880
And you can't keep it as a pet...

454
00:20:14.963 --> 00:20:18.175
because they die when you separate them
from their host.

455
00:20:18.592 --> 00:20:19.927
Really? They die?

456
00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.970
Okay. we haven't agreed upon a plan.

457
00:20:22.179 --> 00:20:23.597
We'll find the undead woman.

458
00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:26.391
You study up and don't do anything
until you hear from us.

459
00:20:26.475 --> 00:20:29.686
And. if you lose interest
in the whole project. that's fine. too.

460
00:20:30.395 --> 00:20:31.230
Sweetie?

461
00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:34.107
What? You call your sister sweetie?

462
00:20:34.191 --> 00:20:35.191
Yeah.

463
00:20:35.442 --> 00:20:36.526
That's her last name.

464
00:20:36.818 --> 00:20:39.029
Yeah. I'm married to Ken Sweetie.

465
00:20:39.154 --> 00:20:40.489
Yeah. What's your problem?

466
00:20:40.572 --> 00:20:42.407
- I don't have a problem.
- Okay. then.

467
00:20:42.991 --> 00:20:43.991
Sweetie?

468
00:20:46.995 --> 00:20:50.082
Mr. Ball Legs is dying
'cause he's not with Ramona.

469
00:20:50.165 --> 00:20:51.375
That is so sad.

470
00:20:51.458 --> 00:20:55.087
Okay. but I don't know if Mr. Ball Legs
is our biggest problem right now.

471
00:20:56.296 --> 00:20:59.424
We can't let him die.
I'm going to call Ramona

472
00:20:59.508 --> 00:21:01.718
and see if she'll come down
from Seattle and get him.

473
00:21:01.843 --> 00:21:03.443
Let's put a pin on the Ramona discussion

474
00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.390
until we figure out
how we're going to find Tommy

475
00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.266
and undead realtor who isn't you.

476
00:21:07.891 --> 00:21:09.434
Well. what if we make one up?

477
00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:10.977
Ooh. I like it.

478
00:21:11.061 --> 00:21:12.229
I get to pick the name.

479
00:21:12.354 --> 00:21:13.981
Hold on. Maybe I want to...

480
00:21:14.064 --> 00:21:15.732
Rosemary Sinclair.

481
00:21:16.066 --> 00:21:17.651
Shit. that's good.

482
00:21:21.989 --> 00:21:24.825
Ladies and gentlemen. I give you...

483
00:21:25.158 --> 00:21:26.868
Rosemary Sinclair.

484
00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:28.870
The undead realtor of Santa Clarita.

485
00:21:29.079 --> 00:21:31.206
Wow. Nice fake website.

486
00:21:31.623 --> 00:21:33.375
I'd buy a house from the Sinclairs.

487
00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:34.458
It's a stock photo.

488
00:21:34.543 --> 00:21:36.103
There's also one of them
washing the dog

489
00:21:36.169 --> 00:21:38.755
and one of Rosemary
getting bad news over the phone.

490
00:21:39.172 --> 00:21:41.717
I found a motel near the airport...

491
00:21:42.092 --> 00:21:44.720
where we can book a room
for Mr. and Mrs. Sinclair.

492
00:21:44.886 --> 00:21:48.140
Great. Let's tell Tommy they stayed there
the night before they skipped town.

493
00:21:48.265 --> 00:21:51.643
Because they heard the Knights of Serbia
were closing in on them.

494
00:21:51.727 --> 00:21:53.312
And we confirmed Rosemary's undead

495
00:21:53.395 --> 00:21:55.772
because we found body parts
in their motel room.

496
00:21:57.649 --> 00:22:00.360
Looks like we're going to make it
through another day.

497
00:22:01.945 --> 00:22:04.072
I just got a little overwhelmed sometimes.

498
00:22:04.614 --> 00:22:05.615
I get it.

499
00:22:06.033 --> 00:22:08.952
The last 24 hours. we could have died
three different ways.

500
00:22:09.036 --> 00:22:10.996
Four. if we count that left turn you made.

501
00:22:11.204 --> 00:22:12.706
But... we're still here.

502
00:22:13.373 --> 00:22:15.917
String a few good days
like this together...

503
00:22:16.084 --> 00:22:17.878
Pretty soon. you make it through the week.

504
00:22:17.961 --> 00:22:19.212
Then the month. then the year.

505
00:22:19.421 --> 00:22:21.340
Then. who knows?
Someday. a stadium of children

506
00:22:21.423 --> 00:22:23.675
are singing "Happy Birthday"
to Bop bop bop bop bop.

507
00:22:25.052 --> 00:22:26.386
Are you becoming an optimist?

508
00:22:26.511 --> 00:22:28.680
No. I'm still a realist.

509
00:22:29.639 --> 00:22:31.224
I just like our chances.

510
00:22:32.601 --> 00:22:34.144
It's Anne! You guys home?

511
00:22:34.227 --> 00:22:36.104
So she just walks into our house now?

512
00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:37.773
I got you a Costco chicken!

513
00:22:37.939 --> 00:22:39.733
Fuck. yeah. We're in here!

514
00:22:40.817 --> 00:22:41.860
Thank you. Anne.

515
00:22:41.943 --> 00:22:43.820
That was so nice of you.

516
00:22:43.904 --> 00:22:45.906
Sure. Oh!

517
00:22:45.989 --> 00:22:48.429
And I also took care of your little
Chris and Christa problem.

518
00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:49.534
Huh?

519
00:22:49.701 --> 00:22:51.703
I didn't like how they disrespected you.

520
00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:54.539
So I looked them up on the sheriff's
database and it turns out...

521
00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:56.416
they were once convicted of fraud.

522
00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:58.377
And what did you do. Anne?

523
00:22:58.502 --> 00:23:00.837
I leaked it to my friend
at the <i>Valley Journal.</i>

524
00:23:00.921 --> 00:23:03.090
She wrote a pretty scathing story
about them

525
00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:05.717
so they're not gonna be much competition
for you anymore.

526
00:23:07.094 --> 00:23:09.888
Oh. and I also got you some
barbecue sauce. but it's habanero.

527
00:23:09.971 --> 00:23:10.972
So... look out.

528
00:23:15.894 --> 00:23:19.272
I do like the idea of neutering
Chris and Christa.

529
00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:22.109
Me too. But this is kind of extreme.

530
00:23:22.317 --> 00:23:23.819
Wish she would have asked us first.

531
00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:26.947
Definitely. Although. she means well.

532
00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:28.824
And it is just an article.

533
00:23:29.699 --> 00:23:32.452
I still think we should talk to her...
Set some boundaries.

534
00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:42.170
- My goodness. It's her.
- Hello. we're the Randolphs.

535
00:23:42.379 --> 00:23:44.506
I'm George. and this is my wife. Claire.

536
00:23:44.965 --> 00:23:47.050
We've heard of your work
and wanted to meet you.

537
00:23:47.175 --> 00:23:49.177
Oh. do you want to sell your house?

538
00:23:49.845 --> 00:23:51.304
Do you want us to sell our house?

539
00:23:52.013 --> 00:23:53.014
Excuse me?

540
00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:56.059
We know Anne from church.
She said we shouldn't contact you.

541
00:23:56.143 --> 00:23:59.104
but we... just had to witness
God's messenger on Earth.

542
00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:02.940
Oh...

543
00:24:03.275 --> 00:24:05.026
Could you give us a moment?

544
00:24:08.447 --> 00:24:09.698
- Fuck!
- Shit!

545
00:24:11.032 --> 00:24:12.492
Oh. we have to fire Anne.

546
00:24:12.868 --> 00:24:15.287
Yeah... before she does any more damage.

547
00:24:18.373 --> 00:24:20.584
Whoa. I think I found the undead woman.

548
00:24:20.792 --> 00:24:21.792
What?

549
00:24:21.918 --> 00:24:23.545
Realtor couple in Santa Clarita.

550
00:24:23.628 --> 00:24:26.006
He's tall. she's blonde. Look familiar?

551
00:24:26.089 --> 00:24:28.133
Holy shit! That's them.

552
00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.637
Those are the people from the clam farm.
I'm sure of it.

553
00:24:32.721 --> 00:24:37.309
Sleep well. Christa Caldwell.
because tomorrow you die.

554
00:24:37.809 --> 00:24:38.809
Really?

555
00:24:39.269 --> 00:24:41.229
You're just jealous. You didn't say it.

556
00:24:42.305 --> 00:25:42.470
